# Distribution / packaging.
# **Anchored to the repository root.** Every one of these is the Python packaging
# convention for a directory *beside setup.py*, and unanchored they match anywhere in the
# tree: `lib/` was silently ignoring `web/src/lib/` -- the whole API client and four
# utilities -- and `dist/` was ignoring `web/dist/`, the built SPA that is committed on
# purpose so a demo needs no npm. A frontend that builds to `dist/` is not a Python
# packaging artefact, and a pattern that cannot tell the two apart is a pattern that loses
# files. Found by a worker whose new test file under `web/src/lib/` did not appear in
# `git status`.
.Python
/build/
develop-eggs/
/dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
/lib/
lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

